        "original_id": "05d65721-4e7d-5fb5-829f-5c4b95bd8e26",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Epic Poker League\n- Organizations: Federated Sports + Gaming, World Series of Poker, European Poker Tour\n- People: Jeffrey Pollack, Annie Duke, Matt Savage, Michael McDonald, Vanessa Selbst\n- Roles: Executive Chairman, Commissioner, Tournament Director\n- Topics: poker tournament records, WSOP bracelet\n\nFacts:\n- The Epic Poker League was a series of poker tournaments held in 2011 and organized by Federated Sports + Gaming.\n- In 2004, Annie Duke won a World Series of Poker gold bracelet.\n- Jeffrey Pollack served as Executive Chairman of the Epic Poker League.\n- Annie Duke served as Commissioner of the Epic Poker League.\n- Matt Savage served as Tournament Director of the Epic Poker League.\n- Annie Duke was formerly the leading money winner among women in World Series of Poker history, and Vanessa Selbst later held that title.\n- Michael McDonald became the youngest person to win an event on the European Poker Tour.\n- Michael McDonald became the youngest person to win an event on the Epic Poker League.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
